@*
    The two marks in the header: when the data was collected, and when this HTML was built.

    They are a partial for one reason — the live stream re-sends them. Under a live connection the
    table is rebuilt every time a pass lands, and a header still showing the instant of the first
    paint would have the page contradicting itself: fresh figures below, a three-minute-old
    "collected" above. Both marks are facts about the fragment they sit beside, so both travel with
    it (blueprint §5).

    It reads ViewData rather than taking a model, because it is rendered from the layout, which has
    none, and inventing a model for two timestamps would mean the pair list page — which has no
    collected mark at all — needing one too.

    A page with nothing collected prints a dash here. Never a zero, and never the render time
    standing in for it: those are different facts and one of them is not an observation.

    COLLECTED IS A SPAN, not an instant, and that is the correction this partial exists to carry.
    One stamp used to print the freshest received_at on the page — the healthiest row standing in
    for the whole table, so a page holding one venue frozen three days ago announced itself as
    seconds old — and it read only the price call, on a surface whose entire thesis is that price,
    open interest and the depth sweep are three separate clocks. Both ends are printed, from all
    three calls, and they collapse to one clock only when they really are one instant.

    WHICH OF THOSE THREE SHAPES IT IS, is decided in Models/Stamps.cs and not here. It was decided
    here, in one expression, and it was wrong: the two ends were compared as their FORMATTED clocks,
    and HH:mm:ssZ carries no date, so a three-day span whose ends fell on the same second of the day
    compared equal — the span collapsed, the header printed the freshest end alone, and the oldest
    observation left the DOM with it. That is the original defect back, reintroduced by its own fix,
    in the one place on this surface nothing in CI could read.
*@
@{
    var renderedAt = ViewData["RenderedAt"] as DateTimeOffset?;
    var showCollected = ViewData["ShowCollected"] as bool? ?? false;

    var collected = CollectedStamp.Of(
        ViewData["CollectedFrom"] as DateTime?,
        ViewData["CollectedTo"] as DateTime?);
}
<span class="a-stamps" data-live-region="stamps">
    @if (showCollected)
    {
        <span class="a-stamp">
            <span class="a-stamp-label">Collected</span>
            <span class="a-stamp-value" title="@collected.Title">@collected.Text</span>
        </span>
    }
    <span class="a-stamp">
        <span class="a-stamp-label">Rendered</span>
        <span class="a-stamp-value" title="@Format.Utc(renderedAt?.UtcDateTime)">@Format.UtcClock(renderedAt?.UtcDateTime)</span>
    </span>
</span>
